/-! # Flattening algebraic spaces by an admissible blowup

Source: Stacks Project, More on Morphisms of Spaces, Tag 087E,
lemma-flat-after-blowing-up; Divisors on Spaces, Tag 0862
(blueprint: lem-sfb-space-flattening-by-admissible-blowup).

The restriction over the open is given by an actual cartesian square. The conclusion
retains both the centre and the defining torsion ideal of the strict transform.
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraicSpace

/-- A finite-type quasi-separated space over a qcqs base, flat and locally finitely
presented on a quasi-compact open, has a flat finitely presented strict transform after
a blowup whose finite-type quasi-coherent centre is the unit ideal on that open.
Source: Stacks Project, More on Morphisms of Spaces, Tag 087E,
lemma-flat-after-blowing-up; Divisors on Spaces, Tag 0862
(blueprint: lem-sfb-space-flattening-by-admissible-blowup).

Proof:
1. Quasi-compact affine tests and etale atlas composition show Y is quasi-compact.
   The quasi-separated test calculus makes Y absolutely quasi-separated. The qcqs
   finite-type envelope (lem-sfb-space-finite-type-fp-envelope, Tag 0872) embeds Y
   as a closed subspace i : Y -> Z with Z -> T of finite presentation.
2. Put F = i_* O_Y. Closed-immersion pushforward makes F quasi-coherent and finite
   type, generated by 1. Relative local finite-presentation permanence, base change,
   and lem-sfb-space-closed-structure-finite-presentation show F is finitely presented
   over the inverse image of U. The etale pushforward restriction comparison identifies
   this restriction with the pushforward of O_{Y_U}.
3. On each etale scheme chart A -> U, use that restriction comparison and
   lem-sfb-space-closed-pushforward-relative-flatness to deduce relative flatness of
   F over A from flatness of Y_U -> U. This gives flatness over U by chart tests.
4. Z is quasi-compact by the same atlas argument. Apply
   lem-sfb-space-module-flattening-by-admissible-blowup to Z/T, F and U. It gives a
   finite-type ideal I equal to the unit ideal on U, with the module strict transform
   flat over the blowup and of finite presentation.
5. Choose etale scheme charts A -> T and W -> Z_A. By
   lem-sfb-space-strict-transform-etale-localization, space and module transforms
   restrict to the scheme transforms on these charts. The locally principal supported
   kernel lemma and lem-trf-strict-transform-sheaf-kernel identify the torsion-ideal
   definition with the scheme transform. The scheme closed-immersion transfer
   lem-trf-flattening-closed-immersion-transfer then gives flatness and local finite
   presentation of the transformed closed scheme. Chart tests descend both properties.
6. The strict transform is closed in Y times_T T'. Closed immersions are quasi-compact
   and quasi-separated on scheme tests. Base change and composition retain these
   properties from g. Together with step 5, these are exactly finite presentation.
   The centre from step 4 is U-admissible. -/
theorem exists_flat_finitePresentation_spaceStrictTransform_admissibleBlowup
    {S : Scheme.{u}} (Y T U YU : AlgebraicSpace S) (g : Y ⟶ T) (j : U ⟶ T)
    (hj : IsRepresentableWith (fun _ _ p ↦ IsOpenImmersion p.left) j.hom.hom)
    (gU : YU ⟶ U) (q : YU ⟶ Y)
    (hU : IsPullback q.hom gU.hom g.hom j.hom)
    (hTqc : ∃ (V : Over S) (a : yoneda.obj V ⟶ T.obj.obj),
      CompactSpace V.left ∧ IsEtale a ∧ IsSurjective a)
    (hTqs : IsAbsolutelyQuasiSeparated T)
    (hUqc : ∃ (V : Over S) (a : yoneda.obj V ⟶ U.obj.obj),
      CompactSpace V.left ∧ IsEtale a ∧ IsSurjective a)
    (hgft : MapIsFiniteType g)
    (hgqs : MapIsQuasiCompact (pullback.diagonal g.hom.hom))
    (hgUflat : MapIsFlat gU) (hgUlfp : MapIsLocallyOfFinitePresentation gU) :
    ∃ I : QuasiCoherentIdeal T, (I.val : T.Modules).IsFiniteType ∧
      (∀ V : T.EtaleSite,
        (∃ a : yoneda.obj V.obj.left ⟶ U.obj.obj, a ≫ j.hom.hom = V.obj.hom) →
          idealSectionImage I.val.arrow V = ⊤) ∧
      ∃ (B : BlowupPresentation I) (D : StrictTransformPresentation g I B),
        MapIsFlat (D.inclusion ≫ D.toBlowup) ∧
        MapIsLocallyOfFinitePresentation (D.inclusion ≫ D.toBlowup) ∧
        MapIsQuasiCompact (D.inclusion ≫ D.toBlowup).hom.hom ∧
        MapIsQuasiCompact (pullback.diagonal (D.inclusion ≫ D.toBlowup).hom.hom) := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraicSpace
